nce":0.1871,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Dennis Allen"},{"season":2022,"team":"HOU","distance":0.2199,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2024,"team":"CIN","distance":0.2209,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Lou Anarumo"}]},"overview":{"overview":"The Lions are 5-2 through week 8 of the 2026 season and have outscored opponents 203 to 180. The offense has been carrying the team, ranking 6th in EPA per play while the defense sits 30th in EPA allowed. That record is better than the underlying numbers, which suggests a few close games have gone their way. What sets them apart is the 2nd highest under center rate in the league.","offense":"The Lions have one of the most efficient offenses in the league so far, ranking in the top eight in four of the five main efficiency measures. Their run and pass mix has stayed close to what game situations call for. Their biggest outliers in how they line up are the 2nd highest under center rate and the 2nd lowest shotgun rate in the league. Jared Goff has run the passing game and leaned heavily on Amon-Ra St. Brown, who has drawn 31% of the targets.","defense":"The Lions have one of the worst defenses in the league this season, ranking 25th or worse in four of the five main efficiency measures. Their one bright spot has been the pass rush, which ranks 7th in sack rate. Aidan Hutchinson has been as productive as expected, but the bigger surprise is D.J. Wonnum, who has 5 sacks while playing only 54% of the snaps, after not being a regular on this defense last season. Their scheme has been fairly conventional, and the closest thing to a signature is a blitz rate that ranks 12th lowest in the league.","special":"The Lions have been one of the most aggressive teams on fourth down, going for it on 50% of their short-yardage chances so far. Their kickers have made 92% of field goals, which is well above average. Their salary cap was spread across positions in a fairly typical way. Their receivers were among the oldest in the league.","players":"Jared Goff has played nearly every snap at quarterback and thrown for 1,964 yards. Amon-Ra St. Brown has been the clear top target with 31% of the looks and 571 receiving yards. Jahmyr Gibbs has handled most of the work in the backfield with 84% of the carries. On defense, Aidan Hutchinson leads the team with 5 sacks.","coaching":"Drew Petzing is calling the offense and Kelvin Sheppard is calling the defense. Their offense looks most like the 2023 Texans under Bobby Slowik and the 2025 Bears under Ben Johnson. Their defense looks most like the 2025 Titans under Dennard Wilson and the 2022 Cowboys under Dan Quinn.","trends":"The offense went from 7th in EPA per play in 2025 to 6th so far this season, about where it was. The defense moved from 14th in EPA allowed per play in 2025 to 30th so far this season, a big step back. The biggest change in approach was screen rate, which went from 10% to 8%.","notes":"The 2026 pages are built from data that nflverse updates every week, so they will keep changing until the season ends. Personnel, formations, coverage and pressure numbers are missing for now because that data is only released after the season."}}